{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head 75b491f0329ce69c4d6a0aa07f501a365b67407d, tree 7a46897fa085b23785a4e69133428ce77042450a, on builder/ae1-cs1-shared-archive-20261116, all 56 artifacts, for request bfd68316 under my promise bbaa8850. This verdict names all three implementations: AE-1 (request 0c265d01, promise 43fa0d74, report 48835020, the AE-1 note, primary), CS-1 (request 5759be85, promise 37a3f98e, report 5c2c1a02) and LS-6 (request 564972be, promise 52f2a9b2, report 05fcabe0). It covers the certificate cleanup rider of ruling 77a253b9 under AE-1. `gs review --prepare` resolved all three bindings and reports at this head, with each request closing on the sealed receipt. Main 67280592 is an ancestor.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- The proof read, first as ruling 59767cd8 asks. `ScopeObject.applicationArchiveProofBytes` is a namespace RPC with no HTTP route. It reads the Rules pin from SQL and runs no first-ingress dispatch. `storedApplicationArchiveProof` checks the Rules and job record sizes against `PREPARATION_BOUNDS.metadata` before it reads either record. It checks each retained value's size before it reads the body. It requires one current Rules row for the asked directory and an `active` installation. It returns canonical JSON or one of four closed refusals. `application-archive-reader.ts` selects the v1 or v2 codec from the exact native `install-application` fields, with no fallback.\n- The receiver, `archive-packages.ts` and `archive-identity.ts`. `archiveInstallationIdentity` walks the immutable creator chain from the archived scope's own genesis. Each hop takes one native birth and one exact source entry. It checks `sentBy`, the creation cause digest, the Rules and Membership siblings, and the `application-create` fields. It returns the directory, Rules scope, item, root, definition and the three signed IDs, or `unpackaged`, or nothing. The ancestor, body, byte and RPC counts stop at `APPLICATION_ACT_ADMISSION_BOUNDS`. `proof` then authenticates the Rules birth by its pin, reserves the full reply and fixed sender work before the RPC, and settles at actual UTF-8 bytes. `readApplicationArchiveProof` requires exact canonical bytes, the expected Rules scope, directory and item. `installed` then requires the proof's root, definition and IDs to equal the walked identity, and the seed definition to be one of the signed definitions. `add` requires `recorded-do` with only `restricted@1` and a current `APPLICATION_TRUST` row with the same release and publisher. It checks trust again after the declarations validate. Policies reset at the start of each pass.\n- The provider scope, second. `roomArchiveConfiguration` takes the host, namespace and register roots from `artifactsReadiness` and `hostRegisterScopes`. Target discovery takes the repository from the Directory's own open `repository` row with `archive: \"journal\"`. The Destination must be a child of that Directory, and its branch must name the same Directory and repository. The adapter requires that repository's host and namespace to equal the Worker's configuration. The old directory and repository-name pins are gone, as ruling 59767cd8 set.\n- The driver. A production pass reads any stored terminal state first and prepays the terminal write. It prepares package policy before it decodes the archive row or calls the provider, and it checks `policyCurrent` before each provider step. `ArchivePolicyStopped` and `ArchiveChainLimit` store a bounded terminal reason and keep the confirmed receipt. `ArchivePolicyPending` stays a retry.\n- The Workers. `worker.ts` now owns the shared `DeployedScope`, and `worker.grow.ts` only re-exports it. `GROW_ARCHIVE_CONFIG` and the Text rule leave `wrangler.grow.jsonc`. The Grow-only names in `archive.ts` and `archive-policy.ts` remain as aliases that only tests import.\n- The caps. `JOURNAL_INVENTORY_CEILINGS` in `packages/git` raises `nodes` to 128 and `inputWork` to 134,217,728 under ruling 790afe00, and `ARCHIVE_BOUNDS` reads both values from it. The other four ceilings stay. The foreign-source list grammar stays at 64.\n- The page. `publicationHost` comes from the recorded repository row. A room with no repository or host `none` shows \"No archive: this room has no repository.\" A provider other than `artifacts` shows \"Archive unavailable for this repository provider.\"\n- The rider. `certificate.sh` replaces `rm -f` and `rm -rf` with `unlink` of its own known files and `rmdir` of its two staging directories. It keeps the existing `-ef` identity guard for the published key and certificate. Any leftover entry survives, the script prints one fixed line, and a success exit becomes 1. The collision case proves an unknown file survives.\n- CS-1 and LS-6. The `counter.inguz.space` row equals request 5759be85 exactly. The `lending-shelf.inguz.space` row carries directory `sc_a7fawlxb…` and presentation `sha256:188f7b84…`, as request 564972be names them. Both use item 2 and room origin `https://dap-lending.inguz.workers.dev`. The sandbox maps both through the existing `LENDING` binding, and the `lending.inguz.space` row stays.\n- The documents. `docs/operate-a-service.md` gains \"Verify a room from its archive\" with the clone and replay commands. It states that removing a trust row stops each scope of that release with `application-policy-revoked`, and that restoring the row alone does not clear the stop. `docs/security/entry-points.md` lists the new port and its checks.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Scope. The 56 artifacts name the head, no path repeats, and their paths equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only 67280592 75b491f0`.\n- Gate 3, END 2723f6c0. `/Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-16-ae1-cs1-gate-attempt3/gate.log` has SHA-256 0232ea4e…, and `gate.result.json` has adada1b7…. The log names head 75b491f0 and tree 7a46897f with 0 changed files. Pins passed in 17.5 s. Kernel, Node, Counting, Plain 4891 with 1 skipped and Native 1172 with 2 skipped passed, and its last line is \"gate passed\". The result records exit 0 and `passed`.\n- Witnesses, by source only. `archive-installed.test.ts` registers the \"shared Base\" case from `archive-installed.fixture.ts`, and that case is the request's non-Grow room with an installed package. It confirms, empties the trust setting, stops with `application-policy-revoked` twice with the confirmed coverage unchanged, and runs the clone and the public replay command. The driver cases cover the proof-reason and admission-limit stops.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 19 checked, 0 flagged. `check-notes` gives 0 warnings. `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests.\n\nArchitecture: sound. One adapter serves every room Worker, and each Directory supplies its own repository. Policy comes from two closed sources: the native catalog, checked against `ARCHIVE_NATIVE_DATA`, and the declarations of an authenticated installation. The proof read sits in the Rules scope that holds the signed inputs. The receiver decides trust from the Worker's own setting. The ceiling value lives in Git, the lowest layer that enforces it, and Scope reads it, as ruling c461110c keeps it.\n\nSecurity: no blocking finding.\n\n- The proof read discloses only the signed semantic and release values and the installation record that `install-application` already retained. No credential, token or presentation crosses it. The reply grants nothing alone. The receiver authenticates the chain from the archived scope's own genesis to the installation, and it compares every ID with the signed proof. A digest found elsewhere, or equal declaration bytes in another release, cannot select a policy.\n- The trust check uses the current deployment setting at preparation, at each source and before each provider step. A removed row stops the scope before the next provider call.\n- The provider scope is the Worker's own Artifacts host and namespace. Within that namespace, the repository is the one that the Directory's own row and its Destination branch both name. This head changes no rule that writes that row.\n- The certificate rider removes only files that this run made, and it keeps a stranger's file.\n- The new screen rows are nonsecret and add no binding, route, secret or bucket.\n\nFacts for the planner's dry run:\n\n1. The deployment turns on the archive for every Worker with a wired Artifacts binding and valid register roots. Before this head, only Grow ran it. On its first pass, an installed scope whose release has no row in that Worker's `APPLICATION_TRUST` takes the terminal stop `application-policy-revoked`, and restoring the row later does not clear it. Before the first pass, check that each live installed release has its row. On dap-grow, only Grow 2.0.0 (`482f8605…`) is trusted. The earlier Grow release `71e10ca9…` loses the trust that `GROW_ARCHIVE_CONFIG` gave it.\n2. Each new screen name needs a proxied DNS record in the inguz.space zone unless a wildcard record already serves it. The route `*.inguz.space/*` already covers both names.\n3. Gate 3's Native log has four \"Cannot perform I/O on behalf of a different Durable Object\" lines, and the development run at da8a7337 had two. No test failed. The cause and the owning test are unknown.\n\nSimplification: no required change. A later archive head can remove `growArchiveDriver`, `growArchiveConfiguration` and `growArchivePolicies` from production modules by changing the four test files that import them.\n\nThe AE-1 note at this head still opens with \"Current code is 35de4110… new validation is UNRUN\" and does not record gate 3. It also breaks the repository's writing rule: most of it is compressed shorthand that a reader cannot follow. With 971 B left under its cap, its successor should replace the history with a short statement of what passed at this head and what stays open. That repair can follow this landing.\n\nQualifications that stand: gates 1 and 2 stay FAILED. The witnesses use TEST keys, a scripted peer, clock and scheduler, and they show neither hosted fit nor a general cohort bound. ARC-1 owns the case where a creator walk exceeds the remaining pass budget and reports `limit` on each retry. No DNS, hosted, provider or deployment result follows. This approval authorizes no push, landing, signing or deployment. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:488350207f85e161a69fbc4f027a8e260a0d7bd1","binding":"assigned","head":"75b491f0329ce69c4d6a0aa07f501a365b67407d","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bbaa8850f08365cc1ff86b5485d17b4b792b921c\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:43fa0d748aea541ed335caafb06537adc6803b1b\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:37a3f98ea8703306e51b974fd7454a9350ba6001\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:52f2a9b2307f903d2115469681bfdbfa0e451633\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5083dc18fbe6325954e62f68d507e2aaa22fabcf","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0e19afec375423e0206a9d3bd860c4cd8a64fa8d, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1047b4f42afc355fcc2fc9d12a601b9b7ff57d56, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:13de7fcf75bc38db3683b63cafb2c5b38bffaa80, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2395f9bd0e9e13dd229ec43fec81e8a2ef1de59f, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2e218f40cb0fd265a61ea99cd844ce15b419cc53, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:345844f1be3ff598fe860ce1e78146e98bbb9d6e, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:359c8b4a27037c19c78107e3b120d445002204c5, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3699dc47a8d2f0d0e43d3b780688c8cb4aefcb9e, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f75